### Health check and API conventions (no login needed)
# Click "Send Request" above each request. Requests are separated by ###.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### Health: 200 { status: "ok" } (503 SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE when the DB is down)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Your own request id is echoed in the X-Request-Id header and meta.requestId
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: my-test-123

### An invalid request id is replaced by a generated UUID
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: bad id!

### Unknown route: 404 NOT_FOUND (error envelope)
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Route outside /api: also the 404 envelope
GET http://localhost:3000/foo

### Malformed JSON: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{bad json

### OpenAPI document (Swagger UI: http://localhost:3000/api/docs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs-json
